    16	Required fix: define the fence as code-level interfaces earlier: `PolicyInput` must exclude `is_target/true_idx/gt_idx/target_color/target_bp` unless the arm is diagnostic; `ScoringInfo`/collector objects carry them. Add tests that diagnostic arms are labeled and deployable arms cannot access these fields.
    17	
    18	3. Strangler parity criteria are too weak for “no silent behavior change”.
    19	Problem: P1 accepts “first decision same” on 2 seeds, but current behavior depends on skipped episodes, tick-log ordering, reset semantics, partial files, and scorer coupling.
    20	Evidence: P1 criterion is only first decision equality at `acot_note/1004_code_framework.md:311-313`; current reset carries no seed at `carla_uav_tracking/rollout/policy_server.py:65-67` and `carla_uav_tracking/rollout/remote_policy.py:23-25`; tick logs are aligned to seeds by order because skipped episodes do not reset policy at `carla_uav_tracking/rollout/tick_align.py:1-3`; `opening_cl.py` also zips sorted log episode ids to non-skipped scorer rows at `carla_uav_tracking/rollout/opening_cl.py:36-51`.
    21	Evidence: scorer `commit_k` defaults independently at `carla_uav_tracking/rollout/metrics.py:35-41`, while policy `--commit-k` is separate at `carla_uav_tracking/rollout/policy_server.py:111`.
    22	Required fix: parity should include dry-run exact legacy command/env equality, resolved-config hash echo, per-tick seed-bearing logs, same skipped/failed seed set, scorer/policy `commit_k` binding, and metric equality on imported legacy outputs. Live CARLA parity can tolerate trajectory nondeterminism, but not invocation, seed, or scoring drift.
    23	
    24	4. Offline plan addresses known failures, but compatibility metadata is still under-specified.
