     1	"""Student-policy closed-loop rollout env (experiment-design §7 / training-plan Phase E.5).
     2	
     3	A *fork* of `recording/recorder.py::EpisodeRecorder.run()` (NOT a reuse). Two
     4	differences from the expert data-gen loop, neither expressible by a flag:
     5	
     6	  (1) LOOP INVERSION. The expert picks its action from the GROUND-TRUTH target
     7	      position, so data-gen computes the action BEFORE the frame is exposed
     8	      (recorder.py:167 decide, :188 move, :197 tick, :198 capture). A VLA student's
     9	      only input IS the frame, so it must capture FIRST, then decide. The
    10	      tick/capture/act/move ordering is reversed (see the loop).
    11	
    12	  (2) PRIVILEGED GT IS CONTROL-BYPASSED, SCORE-ONLY. get_target_state(),
    13	      get_distractor_states(), _point_in_frame() feed the SCORER (and, for Option-A
    14	      candidate boxes, the tid head's candidate SET) — never the controller. The
    15	      expert's centroid framing / dead-reckoning / forced blind-pan are dropped.
    16	
    17	This module is deliberately torch-free so it can run inside the CARLA container
    18	(py3.6). The policy (torch/VLM, py3.11) is injected — for cross-container runs it is
    19	a socket stub; for the CARLA-only smoke it is an expert adapter.
    20	"""
    21	
    22	from __future__ import annotations
    23	
    24	import os
    25	import time
    26	from dataclasses import dataclass
    27	
    28	import numpy as np
    29	
    30	from scene.scene_manager import SceneManager
    31	from recording.recorder import EpisodeRecorder   # borrow _create_attached_sensor / _point_in_frame only
